2. In this Order —
“asset” includes the assets of the Sponsorship Trust Fund referred to in Annex I of the Convention and other assets administered by MIGA in furtherance of its objective;
“Chairman” means the person selected as Chairman by the Council of Governors under Article 31(b) of the Convention;
“Convention” means the Convention Establishing the Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency;
“Director” means a member of the Board of Directors mentioned in Article 30 of the Convention;
“Governor” means a member of the Council of Governors mentioned in Article 30 of the Convention;
“member” means a State which is a party to the Convention;
“MIGA” means the Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency established under the Convention;
“President of MIGA” means the President of MIGA mentioned in Article 30 of the Convention.

9.—(1) Each of the following persons enjoys immunity from legal process in respect of acts performed by the person in his or her official capacity:
(a)a Governor and his or her alternate;
(b)a Director and his or her alternate;
(c)the President of MIGA.
(2) Each of the following persons enjoys exemption from taxation on or in respect of salaries, expense allowances and other emoluments paid to him or her by MIGA:
(a)the Chairman;
(b)a Director and his or her alternate;
(c)the President of MIGA.
(3) Each Governor and his or her alternate enjoy exemption from taxation on or in respect of expense allowances paid to him or her by MIGA.
(4) Sub‑paragraphs (2) and (3) do not apply to any person who is a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore.
